# The vendored nav chrome is an EXACT byte copy of the apex Precision pin (build_nav.cjs verifies
# byte-identity against `git show <pin>:<path>`). An EOL conversion would make the working-tree bytes
# differ from the pinned LF bytes and break that verification on a fresh Windows checkout, so these
# are never line-ending-converted — like the served labs/rooms above.
content/vendored/site-nav.json -text
content/vendored/nav-snippet.html -text
public/nav.css -text
public/nav.js -text

# The DDNA science export is an EXACT byte copy of UNI.DDNA tools/public_export's output, and the
# /evidence/ddna/ page asks the visitor's browser to re-hash these files against the export manifest.
# An EOL conversion would change the bytes and fail that check, so they are never converted.
public/evidence/ddna/data/*.json -text
